AU  - Chirag U.
AU  - P. S. Aithal
T2  - Poornaprajna International Journal of Teaching & Research Case Studies (PIJTRCS)
PY  - 2026
DA  - 2026-10-31
DO  - 10.64818/pijtrcs.3107.8494.0075
UR  - https://doi.org/10.64818/pijtrcs.3107.8494.0075
AB  - Purpose: The purpose of this study is to analyse Verizon Communications Inc. as a digital connectivity and technology services company, with special reference to telecommunications, digital connectivity, and network infrastructure. The study aims to examine Verizon’s business activities, strategies, resources, capabilities, financial performance, technological development, and competitive position. It also seeks to identify ways of improving customer satisfaction and addressing changing customer expectations through the adoption of emerging technologies such as 5G, artificial intelligence (AI), Internet of Things (IoT), cloud computing, automation, advanced analytics, and next-generation network solutions. Methodology/Approach: The study adopts a company-analysis case-study approach to examine Verizon Communications Inc. from multiple strategic and business perspectives. The analysis integrates SWOC analysis, ABCD analysis, PESTLE analysis, financial analysis, and technological strategy to evaluate the company’s internal capabilities, external business environment, financial position, and technology adoption. The approach also considers Verizon’s wireless, broadband, 5G, fiber broadband, fixed wireless access, IoT, cloud-based services, network solutions, and advanced security technologies in understanding its role as a digital connectivity business. Findings/Results: The analysis indicates that Verizon’s continued investment in telecommunications, digital connectivity, and network infrastructure is closely associated with its ability to respond to the increasing demand for reliable, secure, and high-speed communication services. The study examines the company’s strengths and weaknesses, external opportunities and challenges, business-environmental factors, financial performance, technological capabilities, and strategic adoption of emerging technologies. The findings further highlight the relevance of technologies such as 5G, AI, IoT, cloud computing, automation, advanced analytics, and next-generation network solutions for enhancing service delivery and addressing evolving customer expectations. Originality/Value: The originality and value of the study lie in combining multiple analytical frameworks to provide an integrated understanding of Verizon Communications Inc. as a digital connectivity and technology services company. By bringing together strategic, environmental, financial, and technological perspectives, the study provides a broader view of Verizon’s business position and technological development. The study also offers practical suggestions for strengthening customer satisfaction and meeting future customer expectations through the effective adoption of emerging technologies in telecommunications, digital connectivity, network infrastructure, and technology services. Type of Paper: Exploratory Research Case Study,
